# Force LF line endings for all text files, regardless of the cloning
# machine's own core.autocrlf setting. Found during Alpha 1.7's
# independent-clone verification: a Windows clone with the (very common,
# Windows-recommended-default) core.autocrlf=true setting converts LF to
# CRLF on checkout, which silently breaks a handful of source-text
# structural tests (test/election-web-surface.consumer.mjs) whose regexes
# match a literal `\n`. Without this file, the SAME clean commit produces
# different bytes — and different test results — depending on who clones
# it. This is the standard, correct fix (normalize line endings in the
# repository itself), not a workaround in individual test regexes.
* text=auto eol=lf
